<newsitem itemid="471917" id="root" date="1997-03-27" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: Liang Court 1996 net profit up 12 pct.</title>
<headline>Liang Court 1996 net profit up 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31 1995</p>
<p>	     (in million of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			14.99  vs   13.43</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	   3.6   vs    3.9</p>
<p>    Final Dividend (cents)	 1.11  vs    1.11</p>
<p>    Turnover			 133.37  vs   87.52</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest   5.82  vs    4.28</p>
<p>    Interest expense		10.89  vs   12.70</p>
<p>    Associates			 6.42  vs   17.03</p>
<p>    Pretax profit		   28.88  vs   23.74</p>
<p>    Tax				 13.78  vs   10.13</p>
<p>    Minorities	  (loss)     0.11  vs    0.18 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries   (gain)     0.79  vs    0.06 (loss)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:	     18 July 1996</p>
<p>    Last date books:		  8 July 1997</p>
<p>Note - Property-based Liang Court Holdings Ltd said the extraordinary item was due to the divestment of a former subsidiary Linag Court-Veldon Pte Ltd.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
